{"agent_id":"pp3g-XXKX-tools-migration-readiness-audit-issue-163-establish","agent_seq":17,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T23:06:36.789077798Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"af6c8a8a-dc4a-434a-9924-a8889389d400","comment_uuid":"b4483e93-1711-49ff-98cb-3b6ab1c8e2c6","author":"pp3g-XXKX-tools-migration-readiness-audit-issue-163-establish","content":"VERDICT — Tools migration readiness audit (read-only, nothing modified)\n\n## 1. CATALOG DELTA — Tools/ vs Tools-backup/\n\nTools/ HEAD = be99438 (1 commit ahead of backup 9fede33). Backup is a snapshot of Jul 15; Tools is stale as of Jul 31 catalog write.\n\n**Committed delta (9fede33..be99438):**\n- ADDED (8 agents): big-pickle, gemini-35-flash, glm5.2-auditor, laguna-general, ling-general, nemotron-general, north-mini-code, north-mini-general\n- REMOVED (1): hy3.md (opencode/hy3-free not whitelisted)\n- MODIFIED (7): TOOLING.md (+69/-), opencode-agent-configuration.md (+147/-), agents/builder.md, mimo-explore, mimo-general, mimo-v2.5, nemotron-verifier (model pins corrected)\n- Knowledge page tooling (hub) is a pointer stub to TOOLING.md, not a mirror — fine.\n\n**UNCOMMITTED working-tree delta (present in Tools/ but NOT in backup, NOT yet cataloged):**\n- M .crosslink/rules/global.md — memory-awareness line (uncommitted!)\n- M scripts/claude — memory-scope wrapper (uncommitted; live ~/.local/bin/claude differs further: has --agent, CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE, --auto, laguna provider)\n- ?? .claude/findings-interrupt-plugin.md (research doc, Jul 27)\n- ?? .opencode/ (command/interrupt.md + node_modules/package.json — interrupt command prototype)\n\n## 2. DRIFT FINDINGS — Tools/ vs ASES/ vs tripn-astro/ (file-by-file)\n\n**Agents (.opencode/agents/, Tools/agents/):** only the 4 project agents exist in all three; 16 global agents live in Tools/ + ~/.config/opencode/agents/ (verified identical).\n- auditor.md: Tools≈tripn (2 diff lines: tripn drops model pin); Tools vs ASES 133 diff lines (ASES has project-specific body)\n- builder.md: Tools vs tripn 6 lines (model+desc); Tools vs ASES 123 lines (mode: primary, external_directory, ASES body)\n- orchestrator.md: Tools vs tripn 64 lines; tripn vs ASES 75 lines — BOTH diverge from Tools; ASES has allowlist + GIT RULE + REPOSITORY DISCIPLINE; tripn has SITE DISCIPLINE + site AGENTS.md\n- reviewer.md: Tools≈tripn (2 lines); Tools vs ASES 99 lines\n- **KEY DRIFT:** Tools/agents/* are the TripN-flavored originals; ASES and tripn .opencode/agents/* have diverged from Tools and from each other. Neither ASES nor tripn mirrors Tools exactly.\n\n**Plugins (.opencode/plugins/):**\n- crosslink-guard.ts: Tools vs ASES 122 diff lines; ASES vs tripn 2 lines (ASES has \"opencode \" prefix, tripn has \"opencode models\"). ASES/tripn carry by_type + resolveAgentType + CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE; Tools plugin LACKS these (stale).\n- orchestrator-guard.ts, rtk-guard.ts: IDENTICAL across all three ✓\n\n**Skills (.claude/skills/):** 18 in Tools, 18 in tripn, 20 in ASES.\n- crosslink-adversarial-review + crosslink-subagent-orchestration: in Tools/skills/ (top-level), ASES/.claude/skills/, ~/.config/opencode/skills/ — IDENTICAL in all; MISSING from tripn (tripn has 18, no cross-link skills).\n- kickoff/SKILL.md: ASES ≠ Tools (task-matched timeouts + progress checkpoints); ASES ≠ tripn (33 lines). Tools and tripn carry the OLD kickoff skill.\n- All other skills IDENTICAL across the three.\n\n**Rules (.crosslink/rules/):** name-level: ASES adds kickoff.md (not in Tools/tripn); tripn has tooling.md rule (not in Tools).\n- Content diffs: global.md (Tools vs ASES 1 line — nohup; tripn vs ASES 2 lines — memory line position + crosslink intervene form), knowledge.md (ASES has Workflow+Related Gotchas; tripn/Tools do not), project.md (all three different — per-project content).\n- sanitize-patterns.txt identical.\n\n**Hooks (.claude/hooks/):** all 7 core hooks (crosslink_config, heartbeat, post-edit-check, pre-web-check, prompt-guard, session-start, work-check) IDENTICAL across all three ✓. tripn adds generate-status.py + stop-session.py (not in ASES/Tools).\n\n**MCP servers (.claude/mcp/):** agent-prompt-server.py, knowledge-server.py, safe-fetch-server.py IDENTICAL across all three ✓.\n\n**Configs:**\n- opencode.json: ASES and tripn both register orchestrator-guard/crosslink-guard/rtk-guard + 4 agents; ASES adds mcp block; tripn none. Tools/.opencode has NO opencode.json (only command/interrupt.md).\n- hook-config.json: ASES vs tripn diverge heavily (sentinel model, comment_discipline, kickoff_verification, signing_enforcement, tracking_mode, allowed_bash \"opencode \" vs \"opencode models\", phase_types); Tools hook-config is the OLD minimal relaxed config.\n- permissions.md: ASES is current (allowlist reflected); tripn permissions.md is STALE — still shows only \"crosslink *\" for orchestrator bash, does NOT reflect the aad266f allowlist that its own orchestrator.md has.\n- SESSION-START.md: ASES vs tripn 103 diff lines (different repos, role-routing §1b in ASES only).\n\n## 3. NEW-TOOLING ADDITIONS TO CATALOG (today, #135/#127/#123 — MISSING from TOOLING.md)\n1. **Watcher**: ASES/tools/kickoff-notify.py + ases-kickoff-notify.service + ases-kickoff-notify.timer (Phase 1 monitor+notify, systemd 15s cadence, state machine, STALLED detection) — committed cb15188, NOT in Tools/, NOT in TOOLING.md\n2. **Opencode request-timeout config**: ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json provider.options {timeout:3600000, headerTimeout:300000, chunkTimeout:300000} for opencode + opencode-go — committed cb15188, NOT in TOOLING.md\n3. **Orchestrator role + allowlist**: orchestrator.md allowlist expansion (ps -o, pgrep, tmux, grep/tail/head, git worktree list, curl -I...) + by_type in hook-config + thin-orchestrator rule (playbook §5.7) — committed aad266f, partially reflected in TOOLING.md §4 (orchestrator-guard.ts listed) but allowlist/thin rule NOT\n4. **Review/dependency discipline (playbook)**: agent-orchestration-playbook.md §5.3 task-matched timeouts, §5.4 checkpoint contract, §5.5 two-repo sync, §5.6 reviewer independence, §6.4 watcher — file tracked in ASES/.crosslink/knowledge + tripn (59-line diff: tripn adds §6.5 hub-refs/§6.6 standing workflow), NOT referenced in TOOLING.md\n5. **Also**: kickoff skill task-matched timeouts (ASES only), memory-awareness global.md line, findings-interrupt-plugin.md + .opencode/command/interrupt.md + interrupt.ts (uncommitted in Tools), knowledge.md Workflow Gotchas (ASES only)\n\n## 4. CONSUMPTION MODEL C — LEAN CORE + OVERLAY SPLIT\n\n**LEAN CORE (versioned, single-source, consumed by all repos — put in Tools/, reference by symlink or copy-on-init):**\n- agents/: 16 global agent defs (mirror of ~/.config/opencode/agents/) + the 4 ROLE agents as TEMPLATES (auditor/builder/orchestrator/reviewer with {repo} placeholder in description/SITE-vs-REPO discipline)\n- .claude/hooks/ (7 core hooks, already identical everywhere)\n- .claude/mcp/ (3 servers, already identical)\n- plugins/: crosslink-guard.ts, orchestrator-guard.ts, rtk-guard.ts (current by_type version — Tools copy is stale, must sync FROM ASES)\n- .crosslink/rules/: language rules + global.md + quality/rigor/knowledge + tracking-{strict,normal,relaxed} + sanitize-patterns (unify the global.md/knowledge.md gotchas into ONE canonical copy)\n- .claude/skills/: the 18-20 skills (kickoff skill must take the ASES task-matched-timeout version)\n- .crosslink/knowledge/: agent-orchestration-playbook.md (canonical = ASES, merge tripn §6.5/§6.6), model-discipline.md, crosslink-fork.md, kickoff-custom-template.md\n- opencode timeout config + watcher (tools/kickoff-notify.py + systemd units) — these are SERVER-level, belong in Tools catalog; installable\n- scripts/claude, scripts/opencode, scripts/crosslink-moe (sync claude from live ~/.local/bin: agent flag, CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE, memory scope)\n\n**PER-PROJECT OVERLAY (in each repo, never in core):**\n- project.md rules (per-repo content)\n- .crosslink/rules/kickoff.md (per-rep